Q: Current test status in xUnit.net A: <p>In xUnit.net v3 the current test outcome is accessible through the new <a href="https://xunit.net/docs/getting-started/v3/whats-new#test-context" rel="nofollow noreferrer">TestContext</a>.</p>
<pre class="lang-cs prettyprint-override"><code>namespace StackOverflow.SampleCode;

public class UnitTest : IDisposable
{
    [Fact]
    public void TestSuccess()
    {
        Assert.True(true);
    }

    [Fact]
    public void TestFailure()
    {
        Assert.True(false);
    }

    public void Dispose()
    {
        TestResult? result = TestContext.Current.TestState?.Result;
    }
}
</code></pre>
<p>The result can be either <code>Passed</code>, <code>Failed</code>, <code>Skipped</code> or <code>NotRun</code>.</p>
<p>For <code>TestSuccess</code> it will be <code>Passed</code> and for <code>TestFailure</code> it will be <code>Failed</code>.</p>
